      {
        "source": "/shopify/webhooks",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "shopifyApp",
          "region": "europe-west1"
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "EVERY other /shopify/* path, not just webhooks. Only /shopify/webhooks was rewritten here, so /shopify, /shopify/callback, /shopify/plan-selected and the rest fell through to the `**` catch-all below and served VERGR'S SPA — which sends an unknown path to /platform, the coin-selling landing page. Verified live before this was added: GET https://vergr.app/shopify returned 200 with the Vergr shell. CLAUDE.md's claim that the legacy /shopify routes still answered was false, and this is what made it true. shopifyApp strips the /shopify prefix and routes internally, so an unknown path gets ITS 404 instead of Vergr's marketing site. Must stay AFTER the webhooks rule: Hosting takes the first match.",
        "source": "/shopify/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "shopifyApp",
          "region": "europe-west1"
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "The bare /shopify entry point. `/shopify/**` does not match a path with no trailing segment.",
        "source": "/shopify",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "shopifyApp",
          "region": "europe-west1"
        }
